  "slug": "soliton-coupled-microresonators-8c84",
  "summary": "Three recent preprints address turnkey soliton start-up, pulse-to-pulse dispersion control, and soliton dynamics in fiber lasers.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is dissipative soliton dynamics, in which localized pulses or states are sustained by a balance of dispersion, Kerr nonlinearity, gain or loss, and external driving. One preprint analyzes turnkey dissipative Kerr soliton generation in self-injection-locked photonic-crystal ring resonators using coupled Lugiato-Lefever equations. A second introduces dissipative erasure, a spectral-filtering and nonlinear-amplification scheme that removes pulse-to-pulse dispersion imbalance in burst-mode ultrafast lasers. A survey chapter reviews temporal solitons in mode-locked fiber lasers, including soliton molecules and dispersion-managed solitons. The items are heterogeneous: the first two are research contributions on different platforms, while the third is a review. What is new is the explicit treatment of turnkey start-up in photonic-crystal microresonators and a spectral-filtering route to dispersion-imbalance removal in burst-mode lasers.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
